WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
London, 1911.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.670
Britain's first gurdwara opens, in Putney.

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.100
For years the Sikh
community here stays tiny.

4
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.880
Then it grows.

5
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:18.080
In the 2021 Census, about 524,000 people
in England and Wales identify as Sikh.

6
00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.640
Most live in a few areas:
Southall and Hounslow,

7
00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.490
Birmingham, Wolverhampton, Leicester.

8
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.960
So why did a faith from
Punjab make its home here,

9
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.880
and what changed as it did?

10
00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:34.210
In this mission, you'll trace where
British Sikhs came from, and when.

11
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.170
Then you'll meet bus workers who campaigned
for the right to wear the turban at

12
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.130
work.

13
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.490
Your mission: find out why
Sikhs settled in Britain,

14
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.510
and what the gurdwara became for them.
